      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/pyfenn/fenn\n\n### Category\n\nPython\n\n### Project Title\n\nFenn is a lightweight Python framework designed to automate the \"boring stuff\" in ML projects so developers can focus on the model.\n\n### Project Description\n\nFenn automates ML boilerplate like config parsing, logging, and tracking. It helps developers focus on models without the setup headache. \n\n### Highlights\n\nUnlike complex configuration libraries (like Hydra) that require steep learning curves, SMLE stands out for its minimalism and speed. It combines configuration management, logging, and experiment tracking into a simple lightweight wrapper\n\n### Example Code\n\n```markdown\nfrom fenn import FENN\nfrom fenn.notification import Notifier\nfrom fenn.notification.services import Discord, Telegram\n\napp = FENN()\nnotifier = Notifier()\nnotifier.add_services([Discord, Telegram])\n\n@app.entrypoint\ndef main(args):\n\n    # 'args' contains your configuration\n    # (read from a fenn.yaml file) \n    message = f\"Training with learning rate: {args['training']['lr']}\"\n\n    # This message will be sent to the user through\n    # discord and telegram\n    notifier.notify(message)\n   \n    # This print will be redirected to a local log file\n    # and to a remote monitoring platform (wandb) \n\n    print(message)\n\n    # Your logic here...\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run()\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\n_No response_",
